---
import MiniSim from '../../components/calc/MiniSim';
import GuideLayout from '../../components/GuideLayout.astro';
import ContentTable from '../../components/ContentTable.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { label } from '../../i18n/nav';
import { facts, src } from '../../lib/facts';
import { uop, uopYear, overtime, PARAMS as P } from '../../lib/engine/pl';
import { formatMoney, formatNumber, pct } from '../../lib/format';
const lang = 'en';
const F = facts(lang);
const $ = (x: number) => formatMoney(x, 0, lang);
const $2 = (x: number) => formatMoney(x, 2, lang);
const H = 168;
const netExtra = (g: number, extra: number) => uop({ gross: g + extra }).net - uop({ gross: g }).net;
const GS = [P.minimum_wage.monthly, 7000, 10000, 15000];
const rows = GS.map((g) => { const a = overtime({ gross: g, hoursInMonth: H, h50: 10, h100: 0 }), b = overtime({ gross: g, hoursInMonth: H, h50: 0, h100: 8 }); return [$(g), $2(a.hourly), $(a.extra), $(netExtra(g, a.extra)), $(b.extra), $(netExtra(g, b.extra))]; });
const o7 = overtime({ gross: 7000, hoursInMonth: H, h50: 10, h100: 0 }); const n7 = netExtra(7000, o7.extra);
const o7b = overtime({ gross: 7000, hoursInMonth: 160, h50: 10, h100: 0 });
const o15 = overtime({ gross: 15000, hoursInMonth: H, h50: 10, h100: 0 });
const y15 = uopYear({ gross: 15000 }), y15o = uopYear({ gross: 15000, months: [...Array(11).fill(15000), 15000 + o15.extra] });
const dec15 = y15o.months[11].net - y15.months[11].net, jan15 = netExtra(15000, o15.extra);
const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much will 10 hours of overtime add to my pay on PLN 7,000 gross?', a: `With ${formatNumber(H, 0, lang)} working hours in the month, your hourly rate is ${$2(o7.hourly)}. Ten overtime hours on ordinary working days, with the ${F.ot50} supplement, add ${$(o7.extra)} gross to your salary, or about ${$(n7)} after contributions and the tax advance. In a 160-hour month the rate rises to ${$2(o7b.hourly)}, so the same overtime is worth ${$(o7b.extra)} gross.` },
  { q: `When is overtime paid at ${F.ot100} in Poland, and when at ${F.ot50}?`, a: `Under article 151¹ of the Labour Code the ${F.ot100} supplement applies to overtime worked at night, on Sundays and public holidays that are not working days in your schedule, and on a day off granted in exchange for working a Sunday or holiday. Any other overtime earns ${F.ot50}. The supplement comes on top of normal pay, so an hour at ${F.ot100} is worth two ordinary hours gross.` },
  { q: 'Why does the same overtime pay less in December than at the start of the year?', a: `Overtime pay is added to that month's salary and taxed with it. If your cumulative taxable base has passed ${F.threshold} by December, the excess is taxed at ${F.pitHigh}. On ${$(15000)} gross, ten overtime hours at the ${F.ot50} supplement leave ${$(jan15)} net in January but only ${$(dec15)} in December.` },
];
---
<GuideLayout lang={lang} id="overtime" breadcrumbLabel={label('overtime', lang)} title={`Overtime Pay Poland ${F.year}: ${F.ot50} and ${F.ot100} Rates After Tax`} h1={`Overtime pay in Poland ${F.year}: what extra hours are worth`}
  description={`Overtime pay in Poland ${F.year}: a ${F.ot50} or ${F.ot100} supplement under the Labour Code. On ${$(7000)} gross, 10 hours add ${$(o7.extra)} gross and ${$(n7)} net. Calculate yours.`}
  intro={`The calculator works out overtime pay including the supplement and shows how much of it you keep after contributions and tax.`}
  resume={`Every overtime hour on a Polish employment contract earns your normal hourly pay plus a supplement: ${F.ot100} for work at night, on Sundays and public holidays, and on a day off granted in exchange for Sunday or holiday work, and ${F.ot50} on any other day (article 151¹ of the Labour Code, Kodeks pracy). On ${$(7000)} gross with ${formatNumber(H, 0, lang)} hours in the month, the hourly rate is ${$2(o7.hourly)}, so ten overtime hours at ${F.ot50} come to ${$(o7.extra)} gross and roughly ${$(n7)} take-home. Overtime pay is part of your salary: ZUS, health contribution and income tax advance are all deducted from it, and in the months after your taxable base passes ${F.threshold} the tax rate rises to ${F.pitHigh}. The calculator divides your salary by the hours in the month, multiplies by the overtime hours and supplement, then converts the whole payslip to net. The table below compares overtime at ${F.ot50} and ${F.ot100} for four salaries.`}
  faqs={faqs}
  related={[{ href: route('hourly', lang), name: label('hourly', lang), description: 'From monthly salary to hourly rate and back.' }, { href: route('annual', lang), name: label('annual', lang), description: 'Net pay for each month, including the second bracket.' }, { href: route('home', lang), name: label('home', lang), description: 'Net pay on your base salary, without extras.' }]}
  sources={[src('labour_code', lang), src('pit_act', lang), src('zus_rates', lang)]}>
  <div data-outil><div data-chrome><MiniSim client:load kind="overtime" lang={lang} href={route('home', lang)} /></div></div>

  <h2>Overtime at {F.ot50} and {F.ot100} on four salaries</h2>
  <p>The example uses ten overtime hours on ordinary working days, or eight hours at night or on a public holiday. The hourly rate is salary divided by {formatNumber(H, 0, lang)} hours; the net figures show how much the transfer grows in a month before the second tax bracket.</p>
  <ContentTable headers={['Gross', 'Rate/h', `10 h at ${F.ot50}`, 'Net', `8 h at ${F.ot100}`, 'Net']} align={['r', 'r', 'r', 'r', 'r', 'r']} rows={rows} highlightRow={1} />
  <p>Roughly {pct(n7 / o7.extra, lang)} of every złoty of overtime reaches your account, whatever the salary, as long as the whole taxable base stays in the first bracket. Eight hours at {F.ot100} pay more than ten at {F.ot50}, because each of them counts double.</p>

  <h2>When the supplement is {F.ot100} and when {F.ot50}</h2>
  <p>The Labour Code lists the cases for the higher supplement. {F.ot100} applies to overtime worked at night, on Sundays and public holidays that are not working days under your schedule, and on a day off granted in exchange for working a Sunday or holiday. Any other overtime, including simply staying late on a Tuesday or Thursday, earns {F.ot50}.</p>
  <p>The supplement is paid on top of normal pay, not instead of it. An hour at {F.ot50} is therefore worth one and a half ordinary hours, and an hour at {F.ot100} is worth two. Polish payslips often show the two parts on separate lines: "wynagrodzenie za godziny nadliczbowe" (pay for the hours) and "dodatek {F.ot50}" or "dodatek {F.ot100}" (the supplement).</p>

  <h2>Where the hourly rate comes from</h2>
  <p>The tool divides your monthly gross by the working hours in the month. The widget assumes {formatNumber(H, 0, lang)} hours, but working time varies from month to month and the rate moves with it: on {$(7000)} gross over 160 hours it becomes {$2(o7b.hourly)}. If your pay includes fixed allowances or is set as an hourly rate, the result may differ from what HR calculates. The calculator also assumes overtime is paid in cash in the same month.</p>
  <p>It does not check whether your overtime stays within working-time limits. That is a matter for working-time rules and your company's regulations, not for the payroll calculation.</p>

  <h2>Overtime, the tax bracket and contributions</h2>
  <p>Overtime pay joins the same taxable base as your salary. Early in the year it is taxed at {F.pitLow}, but for anyone who passes {F.threshold} of taxable base during the year, later overtime is taxed at {F.pitHigh}. On {$(15000)} gross, ten overtime hours leave {$(jan15)} net in January and {$(dec15)} in December. Overtime also brings the crossover month forward, since it raises the cumulative base.</p>
  <p>ZUS and health contributions apply to the full amount until gross pay for the year passes the {F.cap} cap. The calculator counts only overtime pay and its supplement. Other components that separate rules or your company's pay regulations may grant for the same hours are not added.</p>

  <h2>Your hourly rate with different monthly hours</h2>
  <p>Check how the value of an hour's work changes when the month has fewer or more hours.</p>
  <div data-chrome><MiniSim client:load kind="hourly" lang={lang} href={route('hourly', lang)} /></div>
</GuideLayout>
